      "Current selected application and fingerprint",
      "Full resolved owner descriptor bytes",
      "Current support policy and source path containment",
      "Exact native version/snapshot/dirty facts and disk/BOM relation",
      "Private checkpoint revision changed by another process",
      "One owner session and one pending application",
      "Connection quota includes pending output and an older applied draft"
    ],
    "dirtyXml": "No automatic owner disk save. A newer draft typed during application survives the earlier receipt.",
    "headlessBsl": "Core requires a positive caller-owned lock acknowledgement and never requests module disk save. Receipt baseline uses the decoded LF query; the exact CRLF draft remains retained. This is a library/synthetic adapter test, not proof of native input prevention.",
